Sydney Trains invites suitably qualified & experienced companies to tender the delivery and management of Testing, Inspection, Calibration & Servicing (TICS) services for Minor Plant & Equipment (MPE) across its Network Maintenance Division. The service includes >8,000 MPE assets across 8 Network Bases, 3 Network Satellites & associated minor sites across the Sydney rail network. Key outcomes include:

• Improved safety, reliability & regulatory compliance of MPE through effective TICS management & service delivery;

• Network-wide centralised & streamlined TICS activities, subcontractor management, scheduling, reporting & invoicing;

• Accurate, auditable & up-to-date asset records management within the Sydney Trains 4229 Register, including service histories & compliance certification;

• Achieving operational efficiencies & value-for-money through supplier consolidation, economies of scale, open-book management & continuous improvement initiatives;

• Ensuring TICS activities are delivered in accordance with industry standards, OEM requirements & Sydney Trains safety requirements;

• Delivery of a scalable & sustainable service that supports future requirements; and

• Single point accountability for end-to-end TICS management, service delivery, compliance reporting & subcontractor governance.
